## Architecture Overview

### Layer Position

This plan operates entirely in the frontend layer, consuming GraphQL APIs provided by Plan 5. It does not create backend services, repositories, or database schemas. The plan follows the **Siraj three-location split** pattern for dashboard pages.

```
                    ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
                    │            DASHBOARD ROUTE (auth-required)        │
                    │                                                   │
                    │  app/(dashboard)/certificates/                   │
                    │       └─ page.tsx (Server Component)              │
                    │            │                                      │
                    │            ├─► getServerUserContext()              │
                    │            ├─► requirePermissionForPage()        │
                    │            ├─► getTranslations(locale)            │
                    │            └─► <CertificateListContainer />      │
                    │                 │                                 │
                    │                 ├─► useQuery(CERT_LIST)           │
                    │                 │      → Apollo Client            │
                    │                 │      → POST /api/graphql        │
                    │                 │                                 │
                    │                 ├─► useMutation(REVOKE)            │
                    │                 ├─► useMutation(REISSUE)         │
                    │                 ├─► useMutation(DELETE)           │
                    │                 │                                 │
                    │                 ├─► Zustand: certListStore          │
                    │                 │   (filters, pagination,         │
                    │                 │    selection, dialog state)      │
                    │                 │                                 │
                    │                 ├─► <CertificateListView />       │
                    │                 │      ├─ ResponsiveViewSwitch    │
                    │                 │      ├─ Desktop: AppDataGrid    │
                    │                 │      ├─ Mobile: MobileCardList  │
                    │                 │      ├─ DesktopMetricCardGrid    │
                    │                 │      ├─ MobileMetricCardGrid     │
                    │                 │      ├─ FilterBar / FilterDrawer │
                    │                 │      ├─ BatchOperationsBar       │
                    │                 │      ├─ CertificateStatusBadge   │
                    │                 │      ├─ RevokeDialog            │
                    │                 │      └─ ConfirmDialog            │
                    │                 │                                 │
                    │                 └─► Navigation: router.push()        │
                    │                      → /certificates/[id]         │
                    └─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                │
                                ▼
                    ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
                    │           BACKEND (Plan 5 provides)               │
                    │                                                   │
                    │  Pothos Queries:                                  │
                    │    certificates(pagination, filters) → Certificate[] │
                    │    certificateMetrics(filters) → Metrics          │
                    │                                                   │
                    │  Pothos Mutations:                                │
                    │    revokeCertificate(id, reason) → Certificate   │
                    │    reissueCertificate(id) → Certificate           │
                    │    deleteCertificate(id) → Boolean                │
                    │    batchRevoke(ids, reason) → BatchResult         │
                    │    batchReissue(ids) → BatchResult               │
                    │    batchDelete(ids) → BatchResult                │
                    └─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Key Architectural Decision: Three-Location Split

**Decision**: The certificate list page follows the Siraj three-location split pattern used by all dashboard pages.

| Location | Path | Responsibility |
|----------|------|----------------|
| App Router page | `app/(dashboard)/certificates/page.tsx` | Server component — auth guard, locale detection, pass-through |
| Container + ViewModel | `frontend/common/views/dashboard/cert-list/` | Apollo queries, mutations, Zustand store integration, event handlers |
| Switcher | `frontend/common/views/dashboard/cert-list/certListView.tsx` | `createLazyView` + `ResponsiveViewSwitch` — lazy-loads tier views |
| Presentation (Desktop) | `frontend/desktop/views/dashboard/cert-list/certList.desktop.tsx` | PageContainer → PageHeader → DesktopMetricCardGrid → FilterBar + AppDataGrid + BatchOperationsBar |
| Presentation (Mobile) | `frontend/mobile/views/dashboard/cert-list/certList.mobile.tsx` | MobilePageContainer → MobilePageHeader → MobileMetricCardGrid → MobileCardList + filter drawer + FAB |
| Zustand Store | `frontend/common/stores/certListStore.ts` | Filters, page, pageSize, selectedIds, sortModel, searchQuery, dialog state |
| GraphQL Documents | `frontend/common/graphql/sharedDocuments/certificates/certificates.documents.ts` | CertificatesQuery, batch mutations, CertificateCountQuery |

**Rationale**: This enforces the clean separation between server-side auth/locale concerns (App Router), stateful client logic (Container), and pure presentation (tier views). Tier views are swapped via `ResponsiveViewSwitch` and share the same ViewModel from the Container.

**Alternative Considered**: Single monolithic client component at the App Router level. Rejected because it violates layer separation, prevents mobile/desktop isolation, and mixes server and client concerns.

