## Route Design

### Route Structure

```
app/
├── (dashboard)/                    ← Auth-required dashboard group
│   ├── layout.tsx                  ← Dashboard shell (sidebar, header) — already exists
│   ├── certificates/                ← NEW — certificate management
│   │   └── page.tsx                ← Certificate list page
│   └── ...other dashboard pages
```

The certificates page lives under `(dashboard)` so it inherits:
- The dashboard layout (sidebar, header, auth guard)
- The `getServerUserContext()` call for permission scoping
- The locale detection from the dashboard layout
- The theme and MUI providers from the root layout

### App Router Page (`app/(dashboard)/certificates/page.tsx`)

The server component:
- Calls `getServerUserContext()` to get the authenticated user and their permissions
- Calls `requirePermissionForPage(userContext, 'certificates.view')` — redirects to `/dashboard` if denied
- Extracts locale from `getLocale()` (cookie-based, same as other dashboard pages)
- Calls `getTranslations(locale)` to get the dashboard layout strings
- Renders `<CertificateListContainer>` with user context and locale as props
- Does NOT fetch certificate data in the server component (client-side Apollo handles data fetching — allows for loading states, pagination, filters)
- Exports `metadata` object with page title (localized)

**Why not SSR the certificate data?** The certificate list uses client-side Apollo queries because:
1. Pagination, search, and filter state need client-side query lifecycle management
2. Page-number offset pagination requires passing `page` and `perPage` in query variables derived from Zustand state
3. Loading overlays and skeleton states need the `useQuery` lifecycle
4. Batch action mutations need optimistic responses and cache updates via the Apollo cache

---

## GraphQL API Surface

### Queries (Consumed — Provided by Plan 5)

Plan 5 defines the certificate queries and mutations. This plan consumes them.

**Query**: `certificates(input: CertificateListInput!): CertificateListResult`

| Argument | Type | Description |
|----------|------|-------------|
| `input.page` | `Int` | 1-based page number (page-number offset pagination) |
| `input.first` | `Int` | Items per page (match `PaginationArgs.first` from codebase; default 10 = `DEFAULT_CLIENT_PAGE_SIZE`, options: 10, 25, 50) |
| `input.search` | `String?` | Full-text search on certificate number, student name, verification code (uses FTS index from Plan 01) |
| `input.status` | `CertificateStatus?` | Filter by status: `pending`, `issued`, `revoked`, `expired`, `failed` (5 statuses, NO `draft`) |
| `input.studentId` | `String?` | Filter by student (UUID string, matching Plan 02 `CertificateFilters.studentId`) |
| `input.templateId` | `String?` | Filter by template (UUID string, matching Plan 02) |
| `input.categoryId` | `String?` | Filter by category (UUID string, matching Plan 02) |
| `input.issuedAtFrom` | `DateTime?` | Issue date range start (matching Plan 02 `CertificateFilters.issuedAtFrom`) |
| `input.issuedAtTo` | `DateTime?` | Issue date range end (matching Plan 02 `CertificateFilters.issuedAtTo`) |
| `input.sortBy` | `CertificateSortField?` | Sort field: `CREATED_AT`, `ISSUED_AT`, `STUDENT_NAME`, `TEMPLATE_NAME` (snake_case enum per Plan 02 §4) |
| `input.sortOrder` | `SortOrder?` | `asc` or `desc` |

> **CRITICAL — Plan 02 alignment**: Filter field names follow Plan 02 §3 `CertificateFilters`: `studentId` (NOT `recipientId`/`recipientName`), `issuedAtFrom`/`issuedAtTo` (NOT `dateFrom`/`dateTo`). Sort field names follow Plan 02 §4 `CertificateSortField`: `STUDENT_NAME` (NOT `recipientName`), `ISSUED_AT` (NOT `issueDate`). All IDs are UUID strings, NOT integers. `$dateFrom`/`$dateTo` store variables are renamed to `$issuedAtFrom`/`$issuedAtTo` in the GraphQL documents section below.

**Type: CertificateListResult** (page-number offset — NOT relay):

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `items` | `[Certificate]` | One page of certificate objects |
| `pageInfo` | `PageInfo` | `{ currentPage, hasMorePages, lastPage, perPage, total }` |

**Type: PageInfo** (INTER_PLAN_CONTRACTS §8 — page-number offset):

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `currentPage` | `Int` | Current page number (1-based) |
| `hasMorePages` | `Boolean` | Whether more pages exist after current |
| `lastPage` | `Int` | Total number of pages |
| `perPage` | `Int` | Items per page |
| `total` | `Int` | Total items matching current filters |

**Type: Certificate** (list view — subset):

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `id` | `ID` | Certificate ID (Apollo cache normalization — REQUIRED) |
| `certificateNumber` | `String` | Human-readable certificate number |
| `verificationCode` | `String` | Unique verification code |
| `status` | `CertificateStatus` | `pending`, `issued`, `revoked`, `expired`, `failed` (5 values, NO `draft`) |
| `studentName` | `String` | Full name of student recipient (Plan 02 `CertificateReturnType.studentName`, NOT `recipientName`) |
| `issuedAt` | `DateTime?` | Date certificate was issued (Plan 02 `CertificateReturnType.issuedAt`, NOT `issueDate`); null for pending/failed |
| `expiryDate` | `DateTime?` | Expiry date (nullable — may not expire) |
| `createdAt` | `DateTime` | Creation timestamp |
| `template` | `TemplateSummary` | Template info (id, name) |
| `category` | `CategorySummary?` | Category info (id, name) |
| `fileSize` | `Int?` | File size in bytes (Plan 02 `CertificateReturnType.fileSize`; null if not generated) |
| `fileUrl` | `String?` | PDF download URL (null for pending/failed; null for `issued` certs whose PDF storage is stale/missing) |

**Type: CertificateMetrics**:

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `total` | `Int` | Total certificates matching current filters |
| `issued` | `Int` | Count of issued certificates |
| `revoked` | `Int` | Count of revoked certificates |
| `pending` | `Int` | Count of pending certificates |
| `expired` | `Int` | Count of expired certificates |
| `failed` | `Int` | Count of failed certificates |

**Query**: `certificateMetrics(filters: CertificateFilters): CertificateMetrics`

Standalone metrics query used when the list query is paginated but metrics need to reflect the full filtered set. This is cached separately from the list query. Uses `fetchPolicy: 'cache-first'`.

**Mutation**: `batchReissueCertificates(ids: [ID!]!, userContext): BatchResult` — reissue expired/revoked certificates
**Mutation**: `batchDownloadCertificates(ids: [ID!]!, userContext): DownloadResult` — generates a ZIP archive URL containing selected certificate PDFs

### Mutations (Consumed — Provided by Plan 5)

| Mutation | Signature | Description |
|----------|-----------|-------------|
| `revokeCertificate` | `(id: ID!, reason: String!) → Certificate` | Revoke a single certificate |
| `reissueCertificate` | `(id: ID!) → Certificate` | Reissue a revoked or expired certificate |
| `deleteCertificate` | `(id: ID!) → Boolean` | Soft-delete a failed certificate |
| `batchRevoke` | `(ids: [ID!]!, reason: String!) → BatchResult` | Batch revoke |
| `batchReissue` | `(ids: [ID!]!) → BatchResult` | Batch reissue |
| `batchDelete` | `(ids: [ID!]!) → BatchResult` | Batch delete |
| `batchReissueCertificates` | `(ids: [ID!]!) → BatchResult` | Batch reissue (expired/revoked) |
| `batchDownloadCertificates` | `(ids: [ID!]!) → DownloadResult` | Generate ZIP archive of selected certificate PDFs |

**Type: BatchResult**:

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `successCount` | `Int` | Number of certificates successfully processed |
| `failureCount` | `Int` | Number of certificates that failed |
| `failures` | `[BatchFailure]` | Per-certificate error details |

**Type: BatchFailure**:

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `id` | `ID` | Certificate ID |
| `error` | `String` | Translated error message |
| `code` | `String` | Error code (e.g., `INVALID_STATUS_TRANSITION`, `NOT_FOUND`) |

**Type: DownloadResult**:

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `downloadUrl` | `String` | Signed URL for the ZIP archive |
| `expiresAt` | `DateTime` | URL expiration timestamp |
| `fileCount` | `Int` | Number of PDFs included in the ZIP |

### GraphQL Documents

All documents live in `frontend/common/graphql/sharedDocuments/certificates/certificates.documents.ts` (per INTER_PLAN_CONTRACTS §17 — plural path):

| Document Name | Type | Usage |
|---------------|------|-------|
| `CertificatesQueryDocument` | Query | `useQuery` — paginated list with page-number offset input |
| `CertificateCountQueryDocument` | Query | `useQuery` — standalone metrics (`fetchPolicy: cache-first`) |
| `RevokeCertificateMutationDocument` | Mutation | `useMutation` — single revoke |
| `ReissueCertificateMutationDocument` | Mutation | `useMutation` — single reissue |
| `DeleteCertificateMutationDocument` | Mutation | `useMutation` — single delete |
| `CertificatesBatchDeleteMutationDocument` | Mutation | `useMutation` — batch delete |
| `CertificatesBatchReissueMutationDocument` | Mutation | `useMutation` — batch reissue |
| `CertificatesBatchRevokeMutationDocument` | Mutation | `useMutation` — batch revoke (with reason) |
| `CertificatesBatchRedownloadMutationDocument` | Mutation | `useMutation` — batch re-download (ZIP) |

**Convention compliance** (per `frontend/common/graphql/AGENTS.md`):
- All documents include `id` field on every object type for Apollo cache normalization
- Uses `useQuery` (NOT `useLazyQuery`) — stateful query with `fetchPolicy: 'cache-and-network'`
- Import hooks from `@apollo/client/react`
- Naming: `{EntityName}QueryDocument`, `{EntityName}MutationDocument`
- Documents are typed via `TypedDocumentNode` for automatic type inference

