## Certificate List Page — Enhanced Component Descriptions

> The following sections provide detailed specifications for the certificate list page,
> table, grid card, revocation dialog, export dialog, and the enhanced Zustand store.
> These are additive — they complement the existing Component Hierarchy and Zustand Store
> Design sections above.

### A. CertificateListPage Component

**Component**: `CertificateListPage`

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/certificates/list/CertificateListPage.tsx`

**Purpose**: Top-level page component that orchestrates the full certificate list experience.
This is the desktop-oriented page wrapper consumed by the App Router page entry point
(see §Route / App Router). It renders the header, filter bar, view toggle, and whichever
list representation is active (table or grid).

**Layout structure**:

```
<PageContainer>
  └─ <PageHeader>
       ├─ title: "Certificates"
       ├─ subtitle: "Manage all issued certificates"
       └─ actions: <Button> "Generate Certificates" (links to /certificates/generate — Plan 17)
  └─ <FilterBar>
       ├─ <TextField> search (searches recipient name, certificate number, email)
       ├─ <Select> status filter (All, Issued, Revoked, Expired, Pending)
       ├─ <Select> template filter (All + list of templates from TemplatesForFilterQuery)
       ├─ <DateRangePicker> (MUI X Date Pickers — issue date range)
       ├─ <Select> sort (Issue Date, Recipient Name, Certificate Number, Expiry Date)
       └─ <Button> Export (opens CertificateExportDialog)
  └─ <ToggleButtonGroup> view mode (Table | Grid)
  └─ viewMode === 'table' ? <CertificateTable> : <CertificateGrid>
</PageContainer>
```

**Behaviour**:
- On mount, calls `loadCertificates` action on the store.
- Filter changes in the FilterBar dispatch the corresponding store actions; store
  triggers Apollo `useQuery` refetch with updated variables (debounce 300ms for search).
- Sort changes dispatch `setSort`; the table/grid apply the sort server-side.
- Export button delegates to `openExportDialog` on the store.
- "Generate Certificates" button does a `next/link` navigation to `/[locale]/certificates/generate`
  — this route is implemented by Plan 17 (Certificate Generation Dialog/Flow).

**Reuses**:
- `PageContainer` from `frontend/components/ui/`
- `PageHeader` from `frontend/components/ui/`

### B. CertificateTable Component (Primary Table View)

**Component**: `CertificateTable`

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/certificates/list/CertificateTable.tsx`

**Purpose**: Primary list view using the existing `AppDataGrid` component
(see `frontend/components/ui/` and the existing Component Hierarchy above) with pinned
first (checkbox) and last (actions) columns.

**Columns**:

| # | Column Key | Header | Width | Sortable | Content |
|---|------------|--------|-------|----------|---------|
| 1 | `checkbox` | — (select-all) | 48 px | No | Checkbox pinnable left |
| 2 | `certificateNumber` | "Certificate #" | 140 px | Yes | Mono font `<Typography variant="body2" sx={{ fontFamily: 'monospace' }}>` |
| 3 | `recipientName` | "Recipient Name" | 160 px | Yes | Text |
| 4 | `recipientEmail` | "Recipient Email" | 200 px | No | Text (secondary color) |
| 5 | `template` | "Template" | 140 px | No | `template.name` from query relation |
| 6 | `status` | "Status" | 110 px | Yes | `<CertificateStatusBadge status=...>` (uses `StatusBadge` with `category="certificateStatus"` — see §Status Badge Mapping) |
| 7 | `issueDate` | "Issue Date" | 140 px | Yes | Date formatted via `formatDate` |
| 8 | `expiryDate` | "Expiry Date" | 140 px | Yes | Date formatted; "—" if null |
| 9 | `actions` | "Actions" | 160 px | No | Row action icons (see below), pinned right |

**Status badges** — reuse `CertificateStatusBadge` (alias of `StatusBadge` with
`category="certificateStatus"`) — Issued (green/success), Revoked (red/error),
Expired (orange/warning), Pending (blue/info), Failed (grey/default).

**Row actions** (rendered as icon buttons in the `actions` cell):

| Action | Icon | Behaviour |
|--------|------|-----------|
| View | `VisibilityOutlined` | Navigates to `/certificates/[id]` (Plan 18) on single-click |
| Download PDF | `DownloadOutlined` | Triggers PDF download using `fileUrl` from the query |
| Revoke | `BlockOutlined` (destructive — `color="error"`) | Opens `RevokeCertificateDialog` with `[id]` |
| Verify | `OpenInNewOutlined` | Opens the public verification URL in a new tab (anchor `target="_blank" rel="noopener"`). Build from base verification URL + `verificationCode` |

**Features**:

- **Sortable columns**: Clicking a sortable header toggles `asc`/`desc` and dispatches `setSort`.
  The sort is server-side — the query is refetched with the new `sort` variable.
- **Row click**: Clicking anywhere on a row (except on action buttons or checkbox)
  navigates to `/certificates/[id]` (Plan 18). Action buttons stop propagation.
- **Pagination**: `AppDataGrid` handles page-size selector. Rows-per-page options: `[10, 25, 50, 100]`.
  Default page size is 10 (per §Zustand Store Design default). Dispatching `setPageSize`
  refetches the query with the new `perPage`.
- **Bulk selection**: The checkbox column supports select-all-on-page. The header checkbox
  toggles selection for all rows on the current page (`toggleAllOnPage`). Dispatches
  `setSelection(ids)` on the store.
- **Bulk actions bar**: A `BatchOperationsBar` (see existing §Component Hierarchy for
  `BatchOperationsBar`) appears when `selectedIds.size >= 1`:
  - **Download All** — triggers `batchRedownloadCertificates`
  - **Revoke All** — opens `RevokeCertificateDialog` with `Array.from(selectedIds)`
  - **Export Selected** — opens `CertificateExportDialog` with `Array.from(selectedIds)`
  The bar also shows "N selected" using a pluralized label.

**AGENTS.md files to read**: root `AGENTS.md`, `frontend/views/AGENTS.md`,
`frontend/AGENTS.md` (MUI v9 style props, icon names), `frontend/components/ui/AGENTS.md`
(if present) for `AppDataGrid` usage.

### C. CertificateCard (Grid View)

**Component**: `CertificateCard`

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/certificates/list/CertificateCard.tsx`

**Purpose**: Renders a single certificate as a visual card for the grid view. This is the
desktop grid equivalent of the mobile `CertificateCardItem` — reuse the same store and
i18n labels but present a richer layout with preview thumbnail.

**Card layout**:

```
<Card sx={{ display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column', maxWidth: 320 }}>
  ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
  │   Certificate preview thumbnail     │  ← 4:3 aspect ratio, rendered certificate preview
  │                                    │     (use template's preview image or placeholder)
  └─────────────────────────────────────┘
  <CardContent>
    ├─ Certificate number (mono)
    │     <Typography variant="subtitle2" sx={{ fontFamily: 'monospace' }}>
    │       CERT-2024-0001
    ├─ Recipient name
    │     <Typography variant="h6">
    │       Ahmed Hassan
    ├─ <CertificateStatusBadge status={...}>
    ├─ Issue date — Expiry date
    │     <Typography variant="caption" sx={{ mr: 1 }}>2024-01-15</Typography>
    │     <Typography variant="caption">— 2025-01-15</Typography>
    └─ Template name
          <Typography variant="caption" sx={{ color: 'text.secondary' }}>
  </CardContent>
  <CardActions>
    ├─ <IconButton title="View">       View
    ├─ <IconButton title="Download">   Download
    ├─ <IconButton title="Revoke" color="error"> Revoke
    └─ <IconButton title="Verify">    Verify (OpenInNewOutlined)
  </CardActions>
</Card>
```

**Props** — same shape as mobile `CertificateCardItem` (see existing contract in
§Component Interface Contracts):

```typescript
interface CertificateCardProps {
  certificate: CertificateFieldsFragment; // from GraphQL documents
  onView: (id: string) => void;
  onDownload: (id: string) => void;
  onRevoke: (id: string) => void;
  onVerify: (verificationUrl: string) => void;
}
```

**Beacon interaction**:
- The card is wrapped in `<CardActionArea onClick={() => onView(certificate.id)}>` — clicking
  the card body navigates to the detail page (Plan 18).
- The `CardActions` row stops propagation — each `IconButton` triggers its own handler.

**Grid container**: `CertificateGrid` uses `<Grid container spacing={{ xs: 2, md: 3 }}>`.
Each card is wrapped in `<Grid item xs={12} sm={6} md={4} lg={3}>`. Pagination below the grid
uses the same store-driven pagination as the table view — page size selector `[10, 25, 50, 100]`.

### D. RevokeCertificateDialog

**Component**: `RevokeCertificateDialog`

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/certificates/list/RevokeCertificateDialog.tsx`

**Props**:

```typescript
interface RevokeCertificateDialogProps {
  open: boolean;
  certificateIds: string[];             // 1 (single revoke) or N (bulk)
  onClose: () => void;
  onRevoked: (ids: string[]) => void;   // called after successful mutation
}
```

**Content**:

```
<Dialog open={open} onClose={onClose} maxWidth="sm" fullWidth>
  <DialogTitle>
    Revoke Certificate(s)
  </DialogTitle>

  <DialogContent>
    <Alert severity="warning" icon={<WarningAmberOutlined />}>
      You are about to revoke {count} certificate(s). This action cannot be undone.
    </Alert>

    {certificateIds.length > 1 && (
      <List dense sx={{ maxHeight: 200, overflow: 'auto' }}>
        {/* List of all certificate numbers being bulk-revoked */}
      </List>
    )}

    <FormControl fullWidth sx={{ mt: 2 }}>
      <InputLabel>Reason</InputLabel>
      <Select value={reason} onChange={...}>
        <MenuItem value="incorrect-information">Incorrect Information</MenuItem>
        <MenuItem value="fraudulent">Fraudulent</MenuItem>
        <MenuItem value="requested-by-recipient">Requested by Recipient</MenuItem>
        <MenuItem value="academic-violation">Academic Violation</MenuItem>
        <MenuItem value="other">Other</MenuItem>
      </Select>
    </FormControl>

    {reason === 'other' && (
      <TextField
        label="Custom reason"
        required
        multiline
        rows={2}
        fullWidth
        sx={{ mt: 2 }}
      />
    )}

    <FormControlLabel
      control={<Switch checked={notifyRecipient} />}
      label="Notify recipient"
    />
  </DialogContent>

  <DialogActions>
    <Button onClick={onClose}>Cancel</Button>
    <Button
      color="error"
      variant="contained"
      onClick={handleConfirm}
      disabled={reason === 'other' && !customReason}
    >
      Revoke
    </Button>
  </DialogActions>
</Dialog>
```

**Behaviour**:
- On confirm: dispatches `revokeCertificates({ ids, reason, notifyRecipient })` on the store.
  For a single revoke this calls `RevokeCertificateMutation`; for bulk it calls
  `BatchRevokeMutation`.
- After success: calls `onRevoked(ids)` so the parent clears selection and refetches,
  then shows a success toast.
- The dialog is controlled via `revokeDialogOpen` on the store. `onOpenRevokeDialog(ids)`
  sets the target IDs and opens the dialog; `onCloseRevokeDialog` clears the dialog open state
  (IDs persist until the parent clears selection).
- The "Revoke" button is disabled until a reason is selected (and when reason is "Other"
  until the custom reason text is non-empty).

**i18n keys**: `revoke.title`, `revoke.warning`, `revoke.warningSingular`, `revoke.reason`,
`revoke.reason.incorrectInformation`, `revoke.reason.fraudulent`,
`revoke.reason.requestedByRecipient`, `revoke.reason.academicViolation`,
`revoke.reason.other`, `revoke.customReason`, `revoke.notifyRecipient`,
`revoke.confirm`, `revoke.cancel`, `revoke.success`, `revoke.error`.

### E. CertificateExportDialog

**Component**: `CertificateExportDialog`

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/certificates/list/CertificateExportDialog.tsx`

**Props**:

```typescript
interface CertificateExportDialogProps {
  open: boolean;
  certificateIds: string[];   // [] = export all (with current filters); non-empty = export selected
  onClose: () => void;
}
```

**Content**:

```
<Dialog open={open} onClose={onClose} maxWidth="sm" fullWidth>
  <DialogTitle>Export Certificates</DialogTitle>
  <DialogContent>
    <RadioGroup value={format} onChange={...}>
      <FormControlLabel value="csv"          control={<Radio />} label="CSV" />
      <FormControlLabel value="pdf-combined" control={<Radio />} label="PDF (combined)" />
      <FormControlLabel value="pdf-zip"      control={<Radio />} label="PDF (individual ZIP)" />
      <FormControlLabel value="excel"        control={<Radio />} label="Excel" />
    </RadioGroup>

    {(format === 'csv' || format === 'excel') && (
      <FormGroup sx={{ mt: 2 }}>
        <FormControlLabel control={<Checkbox checked={cols.certificateNumber} />} label="Certificate #" />
        <FormControlLabel control={<Checkbox checked={cols.recipient} />} label="Recipient" />
        <FormControlLabel control={<Checkbox checked={cols.email} />}       label="Email" />
        <FormControlLabel control={<Checkbox checked={cols.template} />}    label="Template" />
        <FormControlLabel control={<Checkbox checked={cols.status} />}      label="Status" />
        <FormControlLabel control={<Checkbox checked={cols.issueDate} />}   label="Issue Date" />
        <FormControlLabel control={<Checkbox checked={cols.expiryDate} />}  label="Expiry Date" />
      </FormGroup>
    )}

    {(format === 'pdf-combined' || format === 'pdf-zip') && (
      <FormControlLabel
        control={<Switch checked={includeThumbnails} />}
        label="Include preview thumbnails"
      />
    )}
  </DialogContent>

  <DialogActions>
    <Button onClick={onClose}>Cancel</Button>
    <Button
      variant="contained"
      onClick={handleExport}
      disabled={exporting}
      startIcon={exporting ? <CircularProgress size={20} /> : <DownloadOutlined />}
    >
      {exporting ? 'Exporting…' : 'Export'}
    </Button>
  </DialogActions>
</Dialog>
```

**Behaviour**:
- The `export` button calls `exportCertificates` on the store with the configured format and
  column set. For a non-empty `certificateIds` array, the export is scoped to the selected
  certificates; for an empty array, the export uses the current filters and page state.
- A progress indicator (a `CircularProgress` of `size={20}` inside the button, plus a
  transient snackbar with a `LinearProgress`) represents the in-flight export. For PDF ZIP
  exports this may take longer; the dialog stays open with the spinner until the server
  URL is ready.
- Server response (from Plan 5 export query/mutation) returns a download URL which the client
  opens via `window.open(downloadUrl, '_blank')`.
- The dialog is controlled via `exportDialogOpen` on the store.

**i18n keys**: `export.title`, `export.format.csv`, `export.format.pdfCombined`,
`export.format.pdfZip`, `export.format.excel`, `export.columns`, `export.column.certificateNumber`,
`export.column.recipient`, `export.column.email`, `export.column.template`,
`export.column.status`, `export.column.issueDate`, `export.column.expiryDate`,
`export.includeThumbnails`, `export.confirm`, `export.cancel`, `export.exporting`,
`export.success`, `export.error`.

### F. Zustand Certificate List Store — Enhanced Interface

> The existing `certListStore` already defines the store shape used by the desktop/mobile
> list views (see §Zustand Store Design). The interface below is the **enhanced** form that
> adds dialog state, dispatchers for revoke and export workflows, and the `loadCertificates`
> query action. Where a field collides with the existing store, prefer the existing contract.
> New-only fields are marked with `// NEW`.

```typescript
import type { Certificate } from './certListStore.types'; // existing types from the existing store section

interface CertificateListState {
  // --- Data
  certificates: Certificate[];            // current page items
  totalCount: number;                     // total row count across all pages (from PageInfo.total)
  loading: boolean;                       // Apollo query loading
  error: string | null;                   // Apollo error message (i18n key or raw)

  // --- Filters (existing — already declared in §Zustand Store Design)
  searchQuery: string;
  debouncedSearch: string;                 // debounced (300ms) — used as query variable
  statusFilter: string;                   // 'all' | 'issued' | 'revoked' | 'expired' | 'pending'
  templateFilter: string;                 // 'all' | templateId
  dateRange: [Date, Date] | null;          // issue-date range
  sortBy: string;                         // 'issueDate' | 'recipientName' | 'certificateNumber' | 'expiryDate'
  sortOrder: 'asc' | 'desc';

  // --- View
  viewMode: 'table' | 'grid';             // NEW — toggles between CertificateTable and CertificateGrid
  page: number;                           // 1-based
  pageSize: number;                       // default 10
  selectedIds: string[];                  // current selection (stored as array for easy JSON-logging)

  // --- Dialogs
  revokeDialogOpen: boolean;              // NEW
  revokeTargetIds: string[];              // NEW — IDs targeted for revoke action
  exportDialogOpen: boolean;              // NEW

  // --- Actions: data
  loadCertificates: () => void;           // NEW — triggers the Apollo query refetch using current state

  // --- Actions: filters
  setSearchQuery: (query: string) => void;
  setStatusFilter: (status: string) => void;
  setTemplateFilter: (templateId: string) => void;
  setDateRange: (range: [Date, Date] | null) => void;
  setSortBy: (field: string) => void;
  setViewMode: (mode: 'table' | 'grid') => void;       // NEW
  setPage: (page: number) => void;
  setPageSize: (size: number) => void;

  // --- Actions: selection
  toggleSelection: (id: string) => void;
  setSelection: (ids: string[]) => void;
  clearSelection: () => void;

  // --- Actions: revoke workflow
  openRevokeDialog: (ids: string[]) => void;           // NEW — sets revokeTargetIds and opens dialog
  closeRevokeDialog: () => void;                       // NEW — closes dialog, keeps revokeTargetIds until clearSelection()
  revokeCertificates: (params: {
    ids: string[];
    reason: string;
    customReason?: string;
    notifyRecipient: boolean;
  }) => Promise<void>;                                 // NEW — invokes single or batch revoke mutation

  // --- Actions: export workflow
  openExportDialog: (ids: string[]) => void;           // NEW — pulls current selection or [] for filtered export
  closeExportDialog: () => void;                       // NEW
  exportCertificates: (params: {
    format: 'csv' | 'pdf-combined' | 'pdf-zip' | 'excel';
    columns?: string[];
    includeThumbnails?: boolean;
    certificateIds: string[];                          // [] = use current filters
  }) => Promise<void>;                                 // NEW — triggers export and opens download URL
}

// `Certificate` data shape consumed by the table/grid cards (matches the Apollo query result item).
interface Certificate {
  id: string;
  certificateNumber: string;
  recipientName: string;
  recipientEmail: string;
  templateId: string;
  templateName: string;
  status: 'issued' | 'revoked' | 'expired' | 'pending' | 'failed';
  issueDate: string;
  expiryDate: string | null;
  verificationCode: string;
  verificationUrl: string;
  pdfUrl: string;
}
```

**Notes on migration from existing store**:
- The existing store already declares `searchQuery`, `debouncedSearch`, `page`, `pageSize`,
  `sortField`, `sortOrder`, `statusFilter`, `templateId`, `selectedIds`, `columnVisibility`.
  These new fields (dialog booleans, `viewMode`, revoke/export dispatchers, `loadCertificates`)
  should be merged into the same `CertListStoreState` rather than creating a parallel store.
- Use the existing `Set<string>` selection primitive type for `selectedIds` to keep parity
  with the existing code base; the array form above is for serialisation in dialogue state.
  When the dialog needs the list, convert with `Array.from(selectedIds)`.

---

## Round 4 Enhancement — Production Hardening

> **Scope**: This section extends the certificate list management plan with production-grade
> hardening features. All additions follow the existing three-location split, MUI v9 `sx` prop
> convention, Zustand store pattern, and compile-time i18n system established in earlier rounds.
> New store fields are marked `// R4 NEW` and merge into the existing `CertListStoreState`.

### 4.1 Advanced Filters

#### Design Overview

The current FilterBar supports status, template, date range, and recipient search. Round 4
expands the filter surface to cover all real-world certificate management workflows:

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  FilterBar (Desktop) — Enhanced                                       │
│                                                                       │
│  [Search: ""] [Status ▾] [Date Range 📅] [Template ▾]                 │
│  [Recipient: ""] [Cert #: ""] [Tags ▾] [Logic: AND/OR]                │
│  [Active Filters: N] [Clear All] [Save as Preset ⭐]                 │
│                                                                       │
│  ┌─────────────── Advanced Filter Panel (Collapse/Expand) ─────────┐  │
│  │ Date Range Picker:                                                │  │
│  │   ○ Issued Date   ○ Expiry Date   ○ Created Date                │  │
│  │   [From: 📅] [To: 📅]                                           │  │
│  │ Status Multi-Select:                                              │  │
│  │   ☑ Active   ☐ Revoked   ☐ Expired   ☐ Pending   ☐ Failed     │  │
│  │ Template Selector:                                                 │  │
│  │   [All Templates ▾] (searchable Autocomplete)                    │  │
│  │ Filter Logic:                                                      │  │
│  │   (● AND  ○ OR) — combines all active filters                   │  │
│ └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

#### Date Range Picker

Uses MUI v9 `DatePicker` from `@mui/x-date-pickers` (NOT the deprecated `KeyboardDatePicker`).

**Date type selector** — a `ToggleButtonGroup` with three options:

| Toggle | Store field | GraphQL variable | Description |
|--------|-------------|-----------------|-------------|
| Issued Date | `dateFilterType: "issued"` | `$issuedAtFrom`, `$issuedAtTo` | Filter by `issuedAt` field |
| Expiry Date | `dateFilterType: "expiry"` | `$expiryDateFrom`, `$expiryDateTo` | Filter by `expiryDate` field |
| Created Date | `dateFilterType: "created"` | `$createdAtFrom`, `$createdAtTo` | Filter by `createdAt` field |

```typescript
// R4 NEW — store fields for date range type
dateFilterType: 'issued' | 'expiry' | 'created';  // default: 'issued'
// R4 NEW — expiry date range
expiryDateFrom: string | null;
expiryDateTo: string | null;
// R4 NEW — created date range
createdAtFrom: string | null;
createdAtTo: string | null;
// R4 NEW — date filter type setter
setDateFilterType: (type: 'issued' | 'expiry' | 'created') => void;
```

**Component**: `CertificateDateRangeFilter`

```typescript
// File: frontend/views/dashboard/cert/certificates/list/CertificateDateRangeFilter.tsx
// MUI v9 components: DatePicker from @mui/x-date-pickers, ToggleButtonGroup, Box
// All style props via sx={} — no direct fontWeight/mb/mt on Typography/Box
```

```tsx
<LocalizationProvider dateAdapter={AdapterDayjs}>
  <ToggleButtonGroup
    exclusive
    value={dateFilterType}
    onChange={(_, v) => v && setDateFilterType(v)}
    sx={{ mb: 2 }}
  >
    <ToggleButton value="issued">Issued Date</ToggleButton>
    <ToggleButton value="expiry">Expiry Date</ToggleButton>
    <ToggleButton value="created">Created Date</ToggleButton>
  </ToggleButtonGroup>
  <Box sx={{ display: 'flex', gap: 2, alignItems: 'center' }}>
    <DatePicker
      label={t.fromDate}
      value={fromDate}
      onChange={(v) => setDateRange(v, toDate)}
      slotProps={{ textField: { size: 'small' } }}
    />
    <DatePicker
      label={t.toDate}
      value={toDate}
      onChange={(v) => setDateRange(fromDate, v)}
      slotProps={{ textField: { size: 'small' } }}
    />
  </Box>
</LocalizationProvider>
```

#### Status Multi-Select

Replaces the single-select status dropdown with a multi-select using MUI `Autocomplete` with
`multiple` and `renderTags`:

```typescript
// R4 NEW — store enhancement
setStatusMultiFilter: (statuses: CertificateStatus[]) => void;  // replaces setStatusFilter
statusMultiFilter: CertificateStatus[];  // default: [] (all statuses)
```

```tsx
<Autocomplete
  multiple
  options={CERT_STATUSES}  // ['pending', 'issued', 'revoked', 'expired', 'failed']
  value={statusMultiFilter}
  onChange={(_, v) => setStatusMultiFilter(v)}
  renderTags={(value, getTagProps) =>
    value.map((option, idx) => (
      <Chip
        {...getTagProps({ index: idx })}
        key={option}
        label={t.status[option]}
        size="small"
        sx={{ borderRadius: 2 }}
      />
    ))
  }
  renderInput={(params) => (
    <TextField {...params} label={t.status} placeholder={t.allStatuses} />
  )}
/>
```

#### Certificate Number Search

A dedicated `TextField` for searching by certificate number — distinct from the global search:

```typescript
// R4 NEW — store field
certificateNumberSearch: string;
setCertificateNumberSearch: (value: string) => void;
```

This maps to a new GraphQL input field: `input.certificateNumber` (exact prefix match).

#### Tags Filter

Certificates may carry tags (Plan 5 — `tags: [String!]`). The filter is a multi-select
`Autocomplete` of free-text tags fetched from the backend:

```graphql
query CertificateTags($search: String) {
  certificateTags(search: $search) { tags }
}
```

```typescript
// R4 NEW — store field
selectedTags: string[];
setSelectedTags: (tags: string[]) => void;
```

#### Recipient Name Search

Enhanced from the existing `recipientName` field to support partial fuzzy match:

```typescript
// Existing — enhanced maps to GraphQL $recipientName (ILIKE '%name%')
recipientName: string;
setRecipientName: (name: string) => void;  // already exists — enhanced for R4
```

#### Filter Logic (AND/OR)

A `ToggleButtonGroup` that controls how multiple active filters combine:

```typescript
// R4 NEW — store field
filterLogic: 'AND' | 'OR';  // default: 'AND'
setFilterLogic: (logic: 'AND' | 'OR') => void;
```

This maps to `input.filterLogic` in the GraphQL query — the backend combines matching
predicates with AND or OR. When only one filter is active, the logic toggle is disabled.

#### i18n Keys for Advanced Filters

New keys added to the `filters` section of `CertificateListLabels`:

| Key | Type | Description |
|-----|------|-------------|
| `filters.dateType` | `string` | "Date Type" label |
| `filters.dateTypeIssued` | `string` | "Issued Date" toggle |
| `filters.dateTypeExpiry` | `string` | "Expiry Date" toggle |
| `filters.dateTypeCreated` | `string` | "Created Date" toggle |
| `filters.certificateNumber` | `string` | "Certificate #" search label |
| `filters.tags` | `string` | "Tags" filter label |
| `filters.filterLogic` | `string` | "Combine filters with" label |
| `filters.logicAnd` | `string` | "AND" toggle |
| `filters.logicOr` | `string` | "OR" toggle |
| `filters.savePreset` | `string` | "Save as Preset" button label |
| `filters.presetName` | `string` | Preset name input placeholder |
| `filters.presetIcon` | `string` | Preset icon picker label |
| `filters.defaultPreset` | `string` | "Set as default" switch label |

