### 4.2 Saved Filter Presets

#### Design Overview

Users can save the current filter configuration as a named preset for one-click reapplication.

```
┌─────────── Sidebar Filter Preset List ───────────┐
│                                                    │
│  ★ Saved Presets                                   │
│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │
│  │ 📋 "All Issued (2025)"          [Apply] ✕   │ │
│  │ 🏫 "School A — Expired"          [Apply] ✕   │ │
│  │ ⚠  "Revoked This Month"          [Apply] ✕   │ │
│  │ 🔄 "Pending Review"              [Apply] ✕   │ │
│  │ ➕ Save Current Filters as Preset...          │ │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │
│                                                    │
│  ⊙ Active: "All Issued (2025)"                    │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

#### Preset Data Model

```typescript
// R4 NEW — types
interface FilterPreset {
  id: string;                    // uuid
  name: string;                  // user-provided name
  icon: FilterPresetIcon;        // enum: 'star' | 'warning' | 'school' | 'refresh' | ' list' | 'custom'
  filters: CertFilterSnapshot;   // serialized filter state
  isDefault: boolean;            // applied on page load
  shared: boolean;              // shared with team
  createdBy: string;            // user id
  createdAt: string;            // ISO timestamp
  updatedAt: string;            // ISO timestamp
}

interface CertFilterSnapshot {
  statusMultiFilter: CertificateStatus[];
  templateId: string | null;
  categoryId: string | null;
  recipientName: string;
  certificateNumberSearch: string;
  selectedTags: string[];
  dateFilterType: 'issued' | 'expiry' | 'created';
  dateFrom: string | null;
  dateTo: string | null;
  expiryDateFrom: string | null;
  expiryDateTo: string | null;
  createdAtFrom: string | null;
  createdAtTo: string | null;
  filterLogic: 'AND' | 'OR';
}
```

#### Store Additions

```typescript
// R4 NEW — Zustand store fields
filterPresets: FilterPreset[];
activePresetId: string | null;
presetDialogOpen: boolean;
defaultPresetId: string | null;

// R4 NEW — Zustand store actions
loadFilterPresets: () => Promise<void>;
saveFilterPreset: (name: string, icon: FilterPresetIcon) => Promise<void>;
applyFilterPreset: (presetId: string) => void;
deleteFilterPreset: (presetId: string) => Promise<void>;
setPresetAsDefault: (presetId: string, isDefault: boolean) => Promise<void>;
shareFilterPreset: (presetId: string) => Promise<void>;
openPresetDialog: () => void;
closePresetDialog: () => void;
```

#### Preset Persistence

Presets are persisted server-side via a new GraphQL mutation:

```graphql
mutation SaveFilterPreset($input: SaveFilterPresetInput!) {
  saveFilterPreset(input: $input) { id name icon }
}
mutation DeleteFilterPreset($id: ID!) { deleteFilterPreset(id: $id) }
query FilterPresets { filterPresets { id name icon filters isDefault shared } }
```

The `filters` field is a JSON-encoded `CertFilterSnapshot`. The backend stores it in a
`user_filter_presets` table (Plan 5 range — if deferred, presets can use `localStorage` as a
fallback until the backend is ready).

#### Preset Dialog Component

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/certificates/list/SavePresetDialog.tsx`

```tsx
<Dialog open={open} onClose={onClose} maxWidth="xs" fullWidth>
  <DialogTitle>{t.savePreset}</DialogTitle>
  <DialogContent>
    <TextField
      fullWidth
      label={t.presetName}
      value={name}
      onChange={(e) => setName(e.target.value)}
      sx={{ mt: 1 }}
    />
    <Box sx={{ mt: 2 }}>
      <Typography variant="body2" sx={{ mb: 1 }}>{t.presetIcon}</Typography>
      <ToggleButtonGroup exclusive value={icon} onChange={(_, v) => v && setIcon(v)}>
        <ToggleButton value="star"><StarOutlined /></ToggleButton>
        <ToggleButton value="warning"><WarningAmberOutlined /></ToggleButton>
        <ToggleButton value="school"><SchoolOutlined /></ToggleButton>
        <ToggleButton value="refresh"><RefreshOutlined /></ToggleButton>
        <ToggleButton value="list"><ListOutlined /></ToggleButton>
      </ToggleButtonGroup>
    </Box>
    <FormControlLabel
      control={<Switch checked={isDefault} onChange={(_, v) => setIsDefault(v)} />}
      label={t.defaultPreset}
      sx={{ mt: 2 }}
    />
  </DialogContent>
  <DialogActions>
    <Button onClick={onClose}>{t.cancel}</Button>
    <Button variant="contained" onClick={handleSave} disabled={!name.trim()}>
      {t.save}
    </Button>
  </DialogActions>
</Dialog>
```

#### Default Preset on Page Load

When the page mounts, the container checks `defaultPresetId`. If set, it calls
`applyFilterPreset(defaultPresetId)` before the initial query fires. If no default is set,
all filters start at their factory defaults (same as current behavior).

#### Preset Sidebar

A collapsible panel that renders beside the FilterBar on desktop and above the card list on
mobile (collapsed). Each preset shows its icon, name, Apply button, and delete (✕) button.
The active preset is highlighted with `sx={{ bgcolor: (t) => t.palette.action.selected }}`.

---

### 4.3 Custom Column Selection

#### Design Overview

Users can toggle, reorder, and persist which columns are visible in the AppDataGrid.

```
┌──── Column Toggle Dialog ────────────────────────┐
│                                                    │
│  ☑ Certificate Number    (drag handle)  ↕️        │
│  ☑ Recipient             (drag handle)  ↕️        │
│  ☑ Template              (drag handle)  ↕️        │
│  ☑ Status                (drag handle)  ↕️        │
│  ☑ Issued Date           (drag handle)  ↕️        │
│  ☐ Expiry Date           (drag handle)  ↕️        │
│  ☐ Tags                  (drag handle)  ↕️        │
│  ☐ Created By            (drag handle)  ↕️        │
│                                                    │
│  [Reset to Defaults]              [Apply] [Cancel] │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

#### Column Model

```typescript
// R4 NEW — types
interface CertColumnConfig {
  key: CertColumnKey;
  label: string;
  visible: boolean;
  width: number;            // pixel width — persisted
  order: number;            // display order — persisted
}

type CertColumnKey =
  | 'certificateNumber'
  | 'recipient'
  | 'template'
  | 'status'
  | 'issuedDate'
  | 'expiryDate'
  | 'tags'
  | 'createdBy'
  | 'category'
  | 'verificationCode'
  | 'actions';

// Default columns (visible by default)
const DEFAULT_CERT_COLUMNS: CertColumnKey[] = [
  'certificateNumber', 'recipient', 'template', 'status', 'issuedDate',
];

// Custom columns (hidden by default, user can enable)
const CUSTOM_CERT_COLUMNS: CertColumnKey[] = [
  'expiryDate', 'tags', 'createdBy', 'category', 'verificationCode',
];
```

#### Store Additions

```typescript
// R4 NEW — Zustand store fields
columnConfig: CertColumnConfig[];       // full config with order, width, visibility
columnConfigDialogOpen: boolean;

// R4 NEW — Zustand store actions
toggleColumnVisibility: (key: CertColumnKey) => void;
setColumnOrder: (key: CertColumnKey, order: number) => void;
setColumnWidth: (key: CertColumnKey, width: number) => void;
resetColumnConfig: () => void;          // reset to defaults
openColumnConfigDialog: () => void;
closeColumnConfigDialog: () => void;
```

#### Column Toggle Dialog

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/certificates/list/ColumnConfigDialog.tsx`

Uses `@dnd-kit/sortable` for drag-to-reorder (already a project dependency — check package.json).
Each row is a `SortableItem` with a checkbox and a drag handle:

```tsx
<Dialog open={open} onClose={onClose} maxWidth="sm" fullWidth>
  <DialogTitle>{t.columns}</DialogTitle>
  <DialogContent>
    <DndContext sensors={sensors} collisionDetection={closestCenter}
      onDragEnd={handleDragEnd}>
      <SortableContext items={columnKeys} strategy={verticalListSortingStrategy}>
        {columnConfig.map((col) => (
          <SortableColumnItem
            key={col.key}
            column={col}
            onToggle={() => toggleColumnVisibility(col.key)}
          />
        ))}
      </SortableContext>
    </DndContext>
  </DialogContent>
  <DialogActions>
    <Button onClick={resetColumnConfig}>{t.resetColumns}</Button>
    <Button onClick={onClose}>{t.cancel}</Button>
    <Button variant="contained" onClick={handleApply}>{t.apply}</Button>
  </DialogActions>
</Dialog>
```

#### Column Width Persistence

When the user drags a column resize handle in AppDataGrid, the new width is persisted to
the store via `setColumnWidth(key, width)`. Column config is persisted per-user on the
backend (same `user_preferences` table as presets). If the backend is not ready, the config
falls back to `localStorage` under key `cert-list-columns`.

#### AppDataGrid Column Rendering

The `columnDefs` passed to `<AppDataGrid>` are now dynamically built from `columnConfig`:

```typescript
const columnDefs = useMemo(() => {
  return columnConfig
    .filter((c) => c.visible)
    .sort((a, b) => a.order - b.order)
    .map((c) => buildColumnDef(c.key, c.width, labels));
}, [columnConfig, labels]);
```

---

### 4.4 Export with Column Selection

#### Design Overview

Extends the existing `CertificateExportDialog` (design.md §E) with four export modes and
column selection for CSV/JSON/Excel exports.

```
┌──── Export Dialog (Enhanced) ────────────────────────┐
│                                                       │
│  Export Scope:                                        │
│    (● Current View — respects active filters)         │
│    (○ All Certificates — ignores filters)             │
│    (○ Selected ({count}) — only checked rows)        │
│                                                       │
│  Format:                                              │
│    (● CSV  ○ Excel  ○ PDF  ○ JSON)                    │
│                                                       │
│  Columns (for CSV/Excel/JSON):                         │
│    ☑ Certificate Number                               │
│    ☑ Recipient Name                                   │
│    ☐ Recipient Email                                  │
│    ☑ Template                                         │
│    ☑ Status                                           │
│    ☑ Issued Date                                      │
│    ☐ Expiry Date                                      │
│    ☐ Tags                                             │
│    ☐ Created By                                       │
│                                                       │
│  [ ] Use current column config                         │
│                                                       │
│  [Export]                              [Cancel]        │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

#### Export Scope

| Scope | GraphQL variable | Description |
|-------|-----------------|-------------|
| Current View | `exportScope: "filtered"` | Respects all active filters (status, date, template, tags, search) |
| All Certificates | `exportScope: "all"` | Ignores all filters — exports entire dataset |
| Selected | `exportScope: "selected"` + `ids: string[]` | Only the checked rows |

#### Export Formats

| Format | MIME | Extension | Supports columns |
|--------|------|----------|-----------------|
| CSV | `text/csv` | `.csv` | Yes — column checkboxes |
| Excel (XLSX) | `application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet` | `.xlsx` | Yes — column checkboxes |
| PDF | `application/pdf` | `.pdf` | No — fixed layout |
| JSON | `application/json` | `.json` | Yes — column checkboxes (field selection) |

#### Store Additions

```typescript
// R4 NEW — Zustand store fields
exportScope: 'filtered' | 'all' | 'selected';
exportFormat: 'csv' | 'xlsx' | 'pdf' | 'json';
exportColumns: CertColumnKey[];        // which columns to include
useCurrentColumnConfig: boolean;      // sync export columns with visible grid columns

// R4 NEW — Zustand store actions
setExportScope: (scope: 'filtered' | 'all' | 'selected') => void;
setExportFormat: (format: 'csv' | 'xlsx' | 'pdf' | 'json') => void;
toggleExportColumn: (key: CertColumnKey) => void;
setUseCurrentColumnConfig: (value: boolean) => void;
```

#### Apollo Mutation

```graphql
mutation ExportCertificates($input: ExportCertificatesInput!) {
  exportCertificates(input: $input) {
    downloadUrl
    expiresAt
    fileCount
    format
    fileSize
  }
}

input ExportCertificatesInput {
  scope: ExportScope!
  ids: [ID!]                           # only when scope = SELECTED
  filters: CertificateFilters           # only when scope = FILTERED
  format: ExportFormat!
  columns: [String!]                    # column keys
  includeThumbnails: Boolean
}
```

The mutation returns a signed download URL. The client opens it via
`window.open(downloadUrl, '_blank')` and shows a success toast. For datasets > 1000 rows,
a `LinearProgress` bar indicates estimated time remaining.

---

### 4.5 Bulk Revoke with Reason

#### Design Overview

Enhances the existing `RevokeCertificateDialog` (design.md §D) with multi-select page
awareness, undo capability, and visual revoked indicators.

```
┌──── Certificate Table (Enhanced) ───────────────────────────────────┐
│                                                                       │
│  ☑  Cert Number   Recipient          Status      Issued               │
│  ☑  CERT-2025-001  Ahmed Hassan     ✓ Issued     2025-01-15          │
│  ☐  CERT-2025-002  Sara Mohamed     ✓ Issued     2025-02-01          │
│  ☐  CERT-2025-003  Khalid Rahman    ⚠ [REVOKED]  2025-01-20          │
│                                                                       │
│  ┌─────────── Batch Bar (2 selected) ──────────────────────────────┐  │
│  │ 2 certificates selected    [Revoke All] [Export] [×]            │  │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │
│                                                                       │
│  Select-all checkbox in header: "Select 25 on this page"              │
│  + "Select ALL matching filters (1,230)" link                         │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

#### Multi-Select & Select-All

The AppDataGrid header checkbox has two states:
1. **Page select**: Checks all rows on the current page.
2. **Match-all select**: A secondary link below the checkbox that selects all rows matching
   the current filters (across all pages). This calls a `certificateIds(ids: IDsInput) =>
   [ID!]` query to fetch all matching IDs (capped at 10,000).

```typescript
// R4 NEW — store fields
selectAllAcrossPages: boolean;          // true when user clicked "Select all matching"
totalMatchingIds: number;

// R4 NEW — store actions
selectAllOnPage: () => void;
selectAllMatching: () => Promise<void>;
clearSelection: () => void;              // already exists — enhanced
```

#### Revoke Dialog (Enhanced)

The dialog enforces a **required** reason textarea:

```tsx
<Dialog open={open} onClose={onClose} maxWidth="sm" fullWidth>
  <DialogTitle>
    {count === 1 ? t.revokeTitle : t.revokeBulkTitle}
  </DialogTitle>
  <DialogContent>
    <Alert severity="warning" sx={{ mb: 2 }}>
      {count === 1 ? t.revokeWarningSingular : t.revokeBulkWarning(count)}
    </Alert>
    <Typography variant="body2" sx={{ mb: 1 }}>
      {t.revokeReasonLabel} <span style={{ color: theme.palette.error.main }}>*</span>
    </Typography>
    <TextField
      fullWidth
      required
      multiline
      rows={4}
      value={reason}
      onChange={(e) => setReason(e.target.value)}
      error={reasonSubmitted && !reason.trim()}
      helperText={reasonSubmitted && !reason.trim() ? t.revokeReasonRequired : ''}
      placeholder={t.revokeReasonPlaceholder}
    />
    <Box sx={{ mt: 2 }}>
      <Typography variant="caption" sx={{ mb: 1, display: 'block' }}>
        {t.suggestedReasons}
      </Typography>
      <Stack direction="row" spacing={1} sx={{ flexWrap: 'wrap', gap: 1 }}>
        {SUGGESTED_REASONS.map((r) => (
          <Chip
            key={r.key}
            label={r.label}
            onClick={() => setReason(r.label)}
            size="small"
          />
        ))}
      </Stack>
    </Box>
  </DialogContent>
  <DialogActions>
    <Button onClick={onClose}>{t.cancel}</Button>
    <Button
      variant="contained"
      color="error"
      onClick={handleConfirm}
      disabled={!reason.trim()}
    >
      {t.confirmRevokeCount(count)}
    </Button>
  </DialogActions>
</Dialog>
```

#### Bulk Revoke Confirmation

After the user clicks "Revoke", a confirmation step shows the count:

```
┌──── Confirm Bulk Revoke ─────────────┐
│                                        │
│  ⚠  You are about to revoke 2          │
│     certificates. This action          │
│     cannot be undone (except within     │
│     30 seconds).                       │
│                                        │
│     Reason: "Academic violation"       │
│                                        │
│     [Cancel]         [Confirm Revoke]  │
└────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

#### Undo Within 30 Seconds

After a successful bulk revoke, a snackbar appears with an "Undo" action:

```tsx
<Snackbar
  open={showUndo}
  autoHideDuration={30000}
  onClose={() => setShowUndo(false)}
  message={t.revokeSuccess(count)}
  action={
    <Button color="inherit" size="small" onClick={handleUndo}>
      {t.undo}
    </Button>
  }
/>
```

**Undo mechanism**: The bulk revoke mutation stores the previous status for each certificate
in a return payload `UndoData[]`. If undo is clicked within 30s, a `batchUndoRevoke(ids)`
mutation restores the previous statuses. After 30s, the undo data is discarded server-side.

```graphql
mutation BatchRevokeCertificates($input: BatchRevokeInput!) {
  batchRevokeCertificates(input: $input) {
    successCount
    failureCount
    failures { id code message }
    undoToken          # R4 NEW — JWT token for undo
    undoExpiresAt      # R4 NEW — 30s expiry
  }
}

mutation BatchUndoRevoke($token: String!) {
  batchUndoRevoke(token: $token) {
    successCount
    failureCount
  }
}
```

#### Revoked Certificate Visual Indicator

In the table, revoked rows show:
- A **strikethrough badge**: `<Typography sx={{ textDecoration: 'line-through' }}>`
- Status badge uses `theme.palette.error.main` background
- Row opacity reduced to 0.6: `sx={{ opacity: 0.6 }}`

```tsx
// In the status column renderer
if (row.status === 'revoked') {
  return (
    <Box sx={{ display: 'flex', alignItems: 'center', gap: 1 }}>
      <StatusBadge
        category="certificateStatus"
        status="revoked"
        sx={{ bgcolor: (t) => t.palette.error.main }}
      />
      <Typography variant="caption" sx={{ textDecoration: 'line-through', color: 'text.disabled' }}>
        {row.certificateNumber}
      </Typography>
    </Box>
  );
}
```

---

### 4.6 Full-Text Search

#### Design Overview

The current search field searches certificate number, recipient name, and verification code.
Round 4 extends FTS to cover all searchable fields with debouncer, highlight, recent searches,
and keyboard shortcut.

```
┌──── Search Bar (Enhanced) ────────────────────────────┐
│                                                         │
│  🔍 [Search certificates...          ]  ⌨️ /            │
│                                                         │
│  ┌─── Recent Searches (dropdown) ───────────────┐     │
│  │  🕐 Ahmed Hassan                                │     │
│  │  🕐 CERT-2025-001                               │     │
│  │  🕐 Active certificates                         │     │
│  │  ────────────────────────                       │     │
│  │  Clear recent searches                          │     │
│  └────────────────────────────────────────────────┘     │
│                                                         │
│  Search results (highlight):                            │
│  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │
│  │ CERT-2025-001  **Ahmed** Hassan    Issued      │    │
│  │ CERT-2025-002  Sara **Ahmed**      Pending    │    │
│  └────────────────────────────────────────────────┘    │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

#### Search Fields

| Field | Match type | Weighting |
|-------|-----------|-----------|
| Certificate number | Prefix match | Highest |
| Recipient name | FTS (PostgreSQL `tsvector`) | High |
| Template name | FTS | Medium |
| Tags | Exact match | Medium |
| Verification code | Exact match | Low |

The search query is sent as `input.search: String` which the backend resolves to a
PostgreSQL FTS query across all listed fields using `ts_rank_cd` for relevance ordering.

#### Debouncer (300ms)

Already exists in the container (debounce on `searchQuery` → `debouncedSearch`). Round 4
adds a visual indicator: while typing, the search field shows a small `CircularProgress`
of `size={16}` at the end. Once debounced, the progress stops and results update.

```typescript
// Existing — enhanced with visual debounce indicator
const [searching, setSearching] = useState(false);
useEffect(() => {
  setSearching(true);
  const timer = setTimeout(() => {
    setDebouncedSearch(searchQuery);
    setSearching(false);
  }, 300);
  return () => clearTimeout(timer);
}, [searchQuery]);
```

```tsx
<TextField
  value={searchQuery}
  onChange={(e) => setSearchQuery(e.target.value)}
  InputProps={{
    endAdornment: searching ? (
      <InputAdornment position="end">
        <CircularProgress size={16} />
      </InputAdornment>
    ) : null,
  }}
/>
```

#### Search Highlight

When search results are rendered, matching substrings are highlighted with a `<mark>` tag:

```tsx
function HighlightText({ text, query }: { text: string; query: string }) {
  if (!query.trim()) return <>{text}</>;
  const parts = text.split(new RegExp(`(${escapeRegExp(query)})`, 'gi'));
  return (
    <>
      {parts.map((part, i) =>
        part.toLowerCase() === query.toLowerCase() ? (
          <mark key={i} style={{ bgcolor: 'transparent', fontWeight: 700 }}>
            {part}
          </mark>
        ) : (
          part
        )
      )}
    </>
  );
}
```

#### Recent Searches Dropdown

```typescript
// R4 NEW — store fields
recentSearches: string[];
maxRecentSearches: 8;

// R4 NEW — store actions
addRecentSearch: (query: string) => void;
clearRecentSearches: () => void;
```

Recent searches are stored in `localStorage` (key: `cert-list-recent-searches`) — NOT in the
Zustand persist layer (directory stores are session-scoped per AGENTS.md). On mount, the
container loads recent searches from `localStorage` and populates the store.

The dropdown appears when the search field is focused and `searchQuery` is empty. It shows
the last 8 searches with a clock icon. Clicking a recent search fills the search field.

#### Search Keyboard Shortcut (/)

When the user presses `/`, focus moves to the search field:

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  const handleKeyDown = (e: KeyboardEvent) => {
    if (e.key === '/' && !isTextInputFocused(e.target)) {
      e.preventDefault();
      searchRef.current?.focus();
    }
  };
  window.addEventListener('keydown', handleKeyDown);
  return () => window.removeEventListener('keydown', handleKeyDown);
}, []);
```

A `Tooltip` on the search field shows "Press / to search" with a `Kbd`-styled chip.

#### Search API Spec

```graphql
query Certificates($input: CertificateListInput!) {
  certificates(input: $input) {
    items {
      id
      certificateNumber
      studentName
      verificationCode
      template { id name }
      status
      # FTS highlights (R4 NEW)
      searchHighlights {
        field          # "certificateNumber" | "studentName" | "templateName" | "tags"
        snippet       # text with <mark> tags around match
      }
    }
    pageInfo { currentPage perPage total hasMorePages lastPage }
  }
}
```

**Note**: `searchHighlights` is a new optional field from Plan 5 — if not yet implemented,
highlighting falls back to client-side substring matching.

---

### 4.7 Virtualized Table

#### Design Overview

For datasets exceeding 1,000 rows on a single page, a virtualized table replaces the
standard AppDataGrid for performance.

```
┌──── Virtualized Table (react-window) ────────────────────────────┐
│                                                                     │
│  ┌─ Fixed Header (sticky) ──────────────────────────────────────┐ │
│  │ Cert #     Recipient      Status    Issued       Actions    │ │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │
│                                                                     │
│  ┌─ Virtual Scroll Area ────────────────────────────────────────┐ │
│  │ [Row 0]   CERT-001   Ahmed     Issued    2025-01   [...]   │ │
│  │ [Row 1]   CERT-002   Sara      Pending   —          [...]   │ │
│  │ [Row 2]   CERT-003   Khalid    Revoked   2025-01   [...]   │ │
│  │ ...                                                          │ │
│  │ [Row 999] CERT-1000  Fatima    Issued    2025-06   [...]   │ │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │
│                                                                     │
│  Showing 1-1000 of 1,230  [Virtual] [Pagination]                   │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

#### Threshold

Virtualization activates when `pageInfo.total > 1000` AND the user selects "Virtual" mode
from a toggle at the bottom of the table:

```typescript
// R4 NEW — store field
tableMode: 'paginated' | 'virtualized';  // default: 'paginated'
```

When `tableMode` is `'virtualized'`, the backend returns all matching rows in a single query
(uncapped page size) and the client renders via `react-window`.

#### react-window Integration

**File**: `frontend/views/dashboard/cert/certificates/list/VirtualizedCertificateTable.tsx`

```tsx
import { FixedSizeList as List } from 'react-window';
import AutoSizer from 'react-virtualized-auto-sizer';

const VirtualizedCertificateTable = ({ rows, columns, labels }: Props) => {
  const Row = ({ index, style }: { index: number; style: CSSProperties }) => (
    <div style={style}>
      <CertificateTableRow row={rows[index]} columns={columns} labels={labels} />
    </div>
  );

  return (
    <Box sx={{ height: 'calc(100vh - 300px)', minHeight: 400 }}>
      <TableHeader columns={columns} sticky />
      <AutoSizer>
        {({ height, width }) => (
          <List
            height={height}
            width={width}
            itemCount={rows.length}
            itemSize={ROW_HEIGHT}
          >
            {Row}
          </List>
        )}
      </AutoSizer>
    </Box>
  );
};
```

#### Fixed Header on Scroll

The header row is rendered as position sticky:
```tsx
<Box
  sx={{
    position: 'sticky',
    top: 0,
    zIndex: 1,
    bgcolor: (t) => t.palette.background.paper,
    borderBottom: 1,
    borderColor: 'divider',
  }}
>
  {/* column headers */}
</Box>
```

#### Row Height Preservation

Row height is fixed at 52px (comfortable) or 40px (compact) — synced with the grid density
selector (§4.8). Fixed height is required for virtualization performance.

#### Filter Preservation

When switching between paginated and virtualized modes, all active filters are preserved.
The query variables change only in `perPage` (10/25/50 for paginated, unlimited for virtualized).

#### Pagination vs Virtualization Selector

A `ToggleButtonGroup` at the bottom-right of the table:

```tsx
<ToggleButtonGroup
  exclusive
  value={tableMode}
  onChange={(_, v) => v && setTableMode(v)}
  size="small"
>
  <ToggleButton value="paginated">
    <Tooltip title={t.paginatedMode}><ViewListOutlined /></Tooltip>
  </ToggleButton>
  <ToggleButton value="virtualized">
    <Tooltip title={t.virtualMode}><ViewStreamOutlined /></Tooltip>
  </ToggleButton>
</ToggleButtonGroup>
```

---

### 4.8 Grid/Card View Enhancements

#### Design Overview

Enhances the existing grid/card view with sorting, image previews, revoked visuals, hover
actions, and density selector.

#### Sortable Grid

Grid cards can be sorted by date, name, or status:

```tsx
<Box sx={{ display: 'flex', justifyContent: 'flex-end', mb: 2 }}>
  <TextField select size="small" value={gridSortField} onChange={...}>
    <MenuItem value="issueDate">{t.sortByDate}</MenuItem>
    <MenuItem value="recipientName">{t.sortByName}</MenuItem>
    <MenuItem value="status">{t.sortByStatus}</MenuItem>
  </TextField>
</Box>
```

```typescript
// R4 NEW — store field
gridSortField: 'issueDate' | 'recipientName' | 'status';
setGridSortField: (field: 'issueDate' | 'recipientName' | 'status') => void;
```

#### Card Image Preview (Certificate Thumbnail)

Each card shows a thumbnail of the certificate PDF:

```tsx
<Card sx={{ position: 'relative' }}>
  <CardMedia
    component="img"
    height={120}
    image={cert.thumbnailUrl ?? '/placeholder-certificate.png'}
    alt={cert.certificateNumber}
    sx={{ objectFit: 'cover' }}
  />
  {cert.status === 'revoked' && (
    <Box
      sx={{
        position: 'absolute',
        inset: 0,
        bgcolor: 'error.main',
        opacity: 0.3,
        display: 'flex',
        alignItems: 'center',
        justifyContent: 'center',
      }}
    >
      <Typography variant="h6" sx={{ color: 'error.contrastText', fontWeight: 700 }}>
        {t.revoked}
      </Typography>
    </Box>
  )}
  <CardContent>
    {/* card content */}
  </CardContent>
</Card>
```

The thumbnail URL is fetched from `cert.thumbnailUrl` — a new optional field in the
`CertificateFieldsFragment` (Plan 5 — a resized JPEG preview of the PDF first page).

#### Card Dim on Revoked

Revoked cards have reduced opacity and a strikethrough certificate number:

```tsx
<Card sx={{ opacity: cert.status === 'revoked' ? 0.6 : 1, transition: 'opacity 0.2s' }}>
  ...
  <Typography
    sx={{
      textDecoration: cert.status === 'revoked' ? 'line-through' : 'none',
      color: cert.status === 'revoked' ? 'text.disabled' : 'text.primary',
    }}
  >
    {cert.certificateNumber}
  </Typography>
  ...
</Card>
```

#### Card Hover with Quick Actions

On hover, a quick-action overlay appears at the top-right of the card:

```tsx
<Card
  sx={{ position: 'relative', '&:hover .quick-actions': { opacity: 1 } }}
>
  <Box
    className="quick-actions"
    sx={{
      position: 'absolute',
      top: 4,
      right: 4,
      display: 'flex',
      gap: 0.5,
      opacity: 0,
      transition: 'opacity 0.2s',
      bgcolor: 'background.paper',
      borderRadius: 2,
      p: 0.5,
      boxShadow: 2,
    }}
  >
    <IconButton size="small" onClick={() => onView(cert.id)}>
      <VisibilityOutlined fontSize="small" />
    </IconButton>
    <IconButton size="small" onClick={() => onDownload(cert.id)}>
      <DownloadOutlined fontSize="small" />
    </IconButton>
    <IconButton size="small" onClick={() => onRevoke(cert.id)}>
      <BlockOutlined fontSize="small" />
    </IconButton>
  </Box>
  {/* card content */}
</Card>
```

#### Grid Density Selector

A `ToggleButtonGroup` that switches between comfortable and compact density:

```typescript
// R4 NEW — store field
gridDensity: 'comfortable' | 'compact';  // default: 'comfortable'
setGridDensity: (density: 'comfortable' | 'compact') => void;
```

```tsx
<ToggleButtonGroup exclusive value={gridDensity} onChange={(_, v) => v && setGridDensity(v)} size="small">
  <ToggleButton value="comfortable">
    <Tooltip title={t.comfortable}><ViewComfortableOutlined /></Tooltip>
  </ToggleButton>
  <ToggleButton value="compact">
    <Tooltip title={t.compact}><ViewCompactOutlined /></Tooltip>
  </ToggleButton>
</ToggleButtonGroup>
```

In compact mode: card spacing reduces to 8px (from 16px), card height shrinks by 20%, and
thumbnail height is 80px (from 120px).

