### 4.9 Loading & Empty States

#### Design Overview

Production-quality loading and empty states with skeleton rows, progressive loading,
illustrations, and error recovery.

#### Skeleton Table Rows

When `loading` is true (initial load, not refetch), the table renders 10 skeleton rows:

```tsx
{loading && (
  <Box>
    {Array.from({ length: 10 }).map((_, i) => (
      <Box key={i} sx={{ display: 'flex', gap: 2, p: 1.5, borderBottom: 1, borderColor: 'divider' }}>
        <Skeleton variant="rectangular" width={100} height={20} />
        <Skeleton variant="text" width={150} />
        <Skeleton variant="text" width={80} />
        <Skeleton variant="rectangular" width={60} height={24} sx={{ borderRadius: 2 }} />
        <Skeleton variant="text" width={100} />
      </Box>
    ))}
  </Box>
)}
```

#### Progressive Data Loading

When paginating, new rows fade in as they arrive. The `notifyOnNetworkStatusChange: true`
flag on `useQuery` provides a `loading` boolean that is true during refetches. During
refetch, existing rows are NOT replaced with skeletons — instead a subtle `LinearProgress`
bar appears at the top of the table:

```tsx
{loading && !initialLoad && (
  <LinearProgress sx={{ position: 'absolute', top: 0, left: 0, right: 0 }} />
)}
```

#### No Certificates Empty State

When the query returns zero items and there are no active filters:

```tsx
<Stack
  spacing={2}
  alignItems="center"
  justifyContent="center"
  sx={{ py: 8 }}
>
  <Image
    src="/illustrations/empty-certificates.svg"
    alt=""
    width={200}
    height={200}
  />
  <Typography variant="h6">{t.empty.title}</Typography>
  <Typography variant="body2" sx={{ color: 'text.secondary' }}>
    {t.empty.description}
  </Typography>
  <Button variant="contained" startIcon={<AddOutlined />} onClick={onGenerate}>
    {t.generate}
  </Button>
</Stack>
```

#### No Results After Filter

When the query returns zero items but filters are active:

```tsx
<Stack spacing={2} alignItems="center" justifyContent="center" sx={{ py: 8 }}>
  <SearchOffOutlined sx={{ fontSize: 64, color: 'text.disabled' }} />
  <Typography variant="h6">{t.emptyFiltered.title}</Typography>
  <Typography variant="body2" sx={{ color: 'text.secondary' }}>
    {t.emptyFiltered.description}
  </Typography>
  <Button variant="outlined" onClick={clearFilters} startIcon={<ClearOutlined />}>
    {t.clearAll}
  </Button>
</Stack>
```

#### Network Error with Retry

When the query errors:

```tsx
<Stack spacing={2} alignItems="center" justifyContent="center" sx={{ py: 8 }}>
  <CloudOffOutlined sx={{ fontSize: 64, color: 'error.main' }} />
  <Typography variant="h6">{t.error.title}</Typography>
  <Typography variant="body2" sx={{ color: 'text.secondary' }}>
    {t.error.description}
  </Typography>
  <Button variant="contained" startIcon={<RefreshOutlined />} onClick={refetch}>
    {t.error.retry}
  </Button>
</Stack>
```

#### Partial Data Indicator

When some columns are unavailable (e.g., `thumbnailUrl` not generated yet), a subtle
indicator appears:

```tsx
<Tooltip title={t.partialData}>
  <InfoOutlined sx={{ fontSize: 16, color: 'warning.main', ml: 0.5 }} />
</Tooltip>
```

