### 4.10 Accessibility

#### Design Overview

Full WCAG 2.1 AA compliance for the certificate table, filters, and view switches.

#### Table ARIA Roles

The AppDataGrid (and VirtualizedCertificateTable) must include:

```tsx
<Box
  role="grid"
  aria-label={t.aria.certTableLabel}
  aria-rowcount={totalCount}
  aria-colcount={visibleColumns.length}
>
  {/* Header */}
  <Box role="row" aria-rowindex={0}>
    {visibleColumns.map((col) => (
      <Box role="columnheader" aria-sort={getSortAriaValue(col.key)}>
        {col.label}
      </Box>
    ))}
  </Box>
  {/* Rows */}
  {rows.map((row, index) => (
    <Box
      role="row"
      aria-rowindex={index + 1}
      aria-selected={selectedIds.has(row.id)}
    >
      {visibleColumns.map((col) => (
        <Box role="gridcell" aria-label={getCellAriaLabel(col.key, row)}>
          {renderCell(col.key, row)}
        </Box>
      ))}
    </Box>
  ))}
</Box>
```

#### Sort Button ARIA Labels

```tsx
<IconButton
  onClick={onSort}
  aria-label={sortOrder === 'asc' ? t.aria.sortAscending : t.aria.sortDescending}
  aria-sort={sortOrder === 'asc' ? 'ascending' : 'descending'}
>
  {sortOrder === 'asc' ? <ArrowUpwardOutlined /> : <ArrowDownwardOutlined />}
</IconButton>
```

#### Filter Panel Keyboard Navigation

The filter panel is fully keyboard navigable:
- `Tab` moves between filter controls
- `Enter` or `Space` toggles dropdowns and checkbox toggles
- `Escape` closes the filter panel/drawer
- `ArrowDown`/`ArrowUp` navigates within dropdown options

#### Screen Reader for Status Changes

When a certificate is revoked or reissued, an `aria-live` region announces the change:

```tsx
<Box aria-live="polite" sx={{ position: 'absolute', left: -9999 }}>
  {statusAnnouncement}
</Box>
```

The `statusAnnouncement` is set after each mutation:
- Revoke: "Certificate CERT-2025-001 has been revoked."
- Reissue: "Certificate CERT-2025-001 has been reissued."
- Bulk revoke: "2 certificates have been revoked."

#### Focus Management on View Switch

When switching between table and grid views, focus moves to the first element of the new
view:

```tsx
const handleViewSwitch = (mode: 'table' | 'grid') => {
  setViewMode(mode);
  requestAnimationFrame(() => {
    if (mode === 'table') {
      tableRef.current?.focus();
    } else {
      gridRef.current?.focus();
    }
  });
};
```

#### Keyboard Shortcuts

| Shortcut | Action |
|---------|--------|
| `/` | Focus search field |
| `Ctrl+A` | Select all on page |
| `Delete` | Delete selected (if permission) |
| `R` | Open revoke dialog for selected |
| `E` | Open export dialog |
| `1` | Switch to table view |
| `2` | Switch to grid view |

#### i18n Keys for Accessibility

| Key | Description |
|-----|-------------|
| `aria.certTableLabel` | "Certificate list" |
| `aria.sortAscending` | "Sort ascending" |
| `aria.sortDescending` | "Sort descending" |
| `aria.selectedCount` | (count) => "{count} selected" |
| `aria.statusChanged` | (status, certNumber) => "Certificate {certNumber} is now {status}" |
| `aria.viewSwitched` | (mode) => "Switched to {mode} view" |

---

### 4.11 Performance Budgets

#### Design Overview

Strict performance budgets ensure the certificate list remains responsive at scale.

| Metric | Budget | Measurement |
|--------|--------|-------------|
| List render | < 16ms per row | `performance.measure()` in dev mode |
| Filter apply | < 100ms | From state change to re-render |
| Search (debounced) | < 200ms | From debounce fire to results render |
| Export (1000 certs) | < 5s | From button click to download trigger |
| Bundle (cert-list) | < 60KB (gzip) | `next build` analyze output |
| Virtualized table (1000 rows) | < 500ms FCP | First contentful paint of table |

#### Measurement Implementation

```typescript
// File: frontend/views/dashboard/cert/certificates/list/usePerfMetrics.ts
// Dev-only performance measurement hook
export function usePerfMetrics(componentName: string) {
  useEffect(() => {
    if (process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'development') return;
    const start = performance.now();
    return () => {
      const duration = performance.now() - start;
      if (duration > 16) {
        logger.warn(`[Perf] ${componentName} render took ${duration.toFixed(2)}ms`);
      }
    };
  }, [componentName]);
}
```

#### Bundle Pruning

To stay within the 60KB budget:
- `react-window` and `react-virtualized-auto-sizer` are lazy-loaded only when virtualization
  mode is activated (`React.lazy(() => import('./VirtualizedCertificateTable'))`).
- `@dnd-kit/sortable` is lazy-loaded only when the column config dialog opens.
- `@mui/x-date-pickers` is code-split into a separate chunk via dynamic import in the
  filter component.

#### Filter Apply Optimization

Filter changes use `useMemo` to derive new query variables:

```typescript
const queryVariables = useMemo(
  () => ({
    page,
    perPage: pageSize,
    search: debouncedSearch,
    filters: {
      status: statusMultiFilter.length > 0 ? statusMultiFilter : null,
      templateId,
      categoryId,
      recipientName: recipientName || null,
      certificateNumber: certificateNumberSearch || null,
      tags: selectedTags.length > 0 ? selectedTags : null,
      issuedAtFrom: dateFrom,
      issuedAtTo: dateTo,
      expiryDateFrom,
      expiryDateTo,
      createdAtFrom,
      createdAtTo,
      filterLogic,
    },
    sort: { field: sortField, order: sortOrder },
  }),
  [page, pageSize, debouncedSearch, statusMultiFilter, templateId, categoryId,
   recipientName, certificateNumberSearch, selectedTags, dateFrom, dateTo,
   expiryDateFrom, expiryDateTo, createdAtFrom, createdAtTo, filterLogic,
   sortField, sortOrder]
);
```

This `useMemo` prevents unnecessary re-renders when unrelated state changes.

#### Search Optimization

The 300ms debounce is implemented in the container with `useEffect` + `setTimeout`. The
debounced value is fed to `useQuery` `variables.search`. Apollo's `cache-and-network` fetch
policy ensures cached results render immediately (< 200ms) while the network request fetches
fresh data.

---

### 4.12 Real-time Updates

#### Design Overview

Certificate status changes propagate in real-time across all open tabs and users.

#### WebSocket for Status Changes

```
┌──── Real-time Architecture ────────────────────────────────┐
│                                                               │
│  Client (Tab A)                  Server                       │
│  ┌──────────────┐                ┌──────────────┐            │
│  │ Apollo Client │─── WS ───────►│ WebSocket     │            │
│  │ + WS adapter  │               │ Gateway       │            │
│  └──────────────┘                └──────┬───────┘            │
│       │                                 │                      │
│       ▼                                 ▼                      │
│  Apollo cache update            Pub/Sub → DB trigger          │
│  (optimistic + confirming)      ON certificate.status          │
│                                        UPDATE                  │
│                                                               │
│  Client (Tab B)                                              │
│  ┌──────────────┐                                             │
│  │ Same update  │                                             │
│  └──────────────┘                                             │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

The WebSocket connection is managed by a `useCertificateWebSocket` hook:

```typescript
// R4 NEW — hook
function useCertificateWebSocket(certId?: string) {
  useEffect(() => {
    const ws = new WebSocket(`${wsBaseUrl}/certificates`);
    ws.onmessage = (event) => {
      const data: CertWSMessage = JSON.parse(event.data);
      switch (data.type) {
        case 'status_changed':
          apolloClient.cache.updateQuery(
            { query: CertificatesQueryDocument, variables: currentVariables },
            (cached) => {
              if (!cached) return cached;
              return {
                ...cached,
                certificates: {
                  ...cached.certificates,
                  items: cached.certificates.items.map((c) =>
                    c.id === data.certificateId
                      ? { ...c, status: data.newStatus }
                      : c
                  ),
                },
              };
            }
          );
          break;
        case 'certificate_created':
          // Invalidate cache and refetch
          apolloClient.refetchQueries({ include: [CertificatesQueryDocument] });
          break;
        case 'certificate_deleted':
          // Remove from cache
          apolloClient.cache.evict({ id: `Certificate:${data.certificateId}` });
          break;
      }
    };
    return () => ws.close();
  }, []);
}
```

#### Optimistic Updates

All mutations already use optimistic updates (established in Round 1). Round 4 adds
optimistic status changes for the bulk revoke flow:

```typescript
const [batchRevoke] = useMutation(CertificatesBatchRevokeMutationDocument, {
  optimisticResponse: (vars) => ({
    batchRevokeCertificates: {
      successCount: vars.ids.length,
      failureCount: 0,
      failures: [],
      undoToken: '',
      undoExpiresAt: '',
      __typename: 'BatchResult',
    },
  }),
  update: (cache, { data }) => {
    if (!data) return;
    // Update each certificate's status to 'revoked' in the cache
    revokeTargetIds.forEach((id) => {
      cache.writeFragment({
        id: `Certificate:${id}`,
        fragment: gql`fragment RevokedStatus on Certificate { status }`,
        data: { status: 'revoked' },
      });
    });
  },
});
```

#### Stale Data Indicator

When the WebSocket disconnects, the data becomes potentially stale. A small indicator
appears at the top of the table:

```tsx
{wsDisconnected && (
  <Alert severity="info" icon={<SyncProblemOutlined />} sx={{ mb: 2 }}>
    {t.staleDataWarning}
    <Button size="small" onClick={refetch} sx={{ ml: 2 }}>
      {t.refresh}
    </Button>
  </Alert>
)}
```

#### Poll for Updates (Fallback)

When WebSocket is unavailable (or failed), the client falls back to polling:

```typescript
const { data, loading, error, refetch } = useQuery(CertificatesQueryDocument, {
  variables: queryVariables,
  fetchPolicy: 'cache-and-network',
  pollInterval: wsConnected ? 0 : 30000,  // Poll every 30s if WS is down
  notifyOnNetworkStatusChange: true,
});
```

#### New Certificate Notification

When a new certificate is created (via WebSocket `certificate_created` event), a toast
notification appears:

```tsx
<Snackbar open={newCertNotification !== null} autoHideDuration={5000}>
  <Alert severity="success" action={
    <Button size="small" color="inherit" onClick={() => router.push(`/certificates/${newCertId}`)}>
      {t.view}
    </Button>
  }>
    {t.newCertificateCreated}
  </Alert>
</Snackbar>
```

---

### 4.13 Enhanced Zustand Store — Full R4 Interface

> The interface below consolidates all Round 4 additions into the existing
> `CertListStoreState`. Fields marked `// R4 NEW` are added; all others remain from
> earlier rounds. This is the canonical interface for the store after Round 4.

```typescript
interface CertListStoreState {
  // ============================================================
  // EXISTING (Rounds 1–3)
  // ============================================================
  searchQuery: string;
  debouncedSearch: string;
  page: number;
  pageSize: number;
  sortField: CertificateSortField;
  sortOrder: SortOrder;
  statusFilter: CertificateStatus;          // legacy single-select — replaced by statusMultiFilter for R4
  templateId: string | null;
  categoryId: string | null;
  recipientName: string;
  dateFrom: string | null;
  dateTo: string | null;
  selectedIds: Set<string>;
  columnVisibility: Record<string, boolean>;
  viewMode: 'table' | 'grid';
  revokeDialogOpen: boolean;
  revokeTargetIds: string[];
  exportDialogOpen: boolean;

  // ============================================================
  // R4 NEW — Advanced Filters (§4.1)
  // ============================================================
  dateFilterType: 'issued' | 'expiry' | 'created';
  expiryDateFrom: string | null;
  expiryDateTo: string | null;
  createdAtFrom: string | null;
  createdAtTo: string | null;
  statusMultiFilter: CertificateStatus[];
  certificateNumberSearch: string;
  selectedTags: string[];
  filterLogic: 'AND' | 'OR';
  advancedFilterPanelOpen: boolean;

  // ============================================================
  // R4 NEW — Saved Filter Presets (§4.2)
  // ============================================================
  filterPresets: FilterPreset[];
  activePresetId: string | null;
  presetDialogOpen: boolean;
  defaultPresetId: string | null;

  // ============================================================
  // R4 NEW — Custom Column Selection (§4.3)
  // ============================================================
  columnConfig: CertColumnConfig[];
  columnConfigDialogOpen: boolean;

  // ============================================================
  // R4 NEW — Export with Column Selection (§4.4)
  // ============================================================
  exportScope: 'filtered' | 'all' | 'selected';
  exportFormat: 'csv' | 'xlsx' | 'pdf' | 'json';
  exportColumns: CertColumnKey[];
  useCurrentColumnConfig: boolean;

  // ============================================================
  // R4 NEW — Bulk Revoke (§4.5)
  // ============================================================
  selectAllAcrossPages: boolean;
  totalMatchingIds: number;
  undoToken: string | null;
  undoExpiresAt: string | null;
  revokeReason: string;
  revokeReasonSubmitted: boolean;
  showUndoSnackbar: boolean;

  // ============================================================
  // R4 NEW — Full-Text Search (§4.6)
  // ============================================================
  recentSearches: string[];
  maxRecentSearches: number;
  searching: boolean;

  // ============================================================
  // R4 NEW — Virtualized Table (§4.7)
  // ============================================================
  tableMode: 'paginated' | 'virtualized';

  // ============================================================
  // R4 NEW — Grid/Card View (§4.8)
  // ============================================================
  gridSortField: 'issueDate' | 'recipientName' | 'status';
  gridDensity: 'comfortable' | 'compact';

  // ============================================================
  // R4 NEW — Real-time Updates (§4.12)
  // ============================================================
  wsConnected: boolean;
  staleData: boolean;
  newCertNotification: { id: string; number: string } | null;

  // ============================================================
  // R4 NEW — Actions
  // ============================================================
  // Advanced Filters
  setDateFilterType: (type: 'issued' | 'expiry' | 'created') => void;
  setExpiryDateRange: (from: string | null, to: string | null) => void;
  setCreatedDateRange: (from: string | null, to: string | null) => void;
  setStatusMultiFilter: (statuses: CertificateStatus[]) => void;
  setCertificateNumberSearch: (value: string) => void;
  setSelectedTags: (tags: string[]) => void;
  setFilterLogic: (logic: 'AND' | 'OR') => void;
  setAdvancedFilterPanelOpen: (open: boolean) => void;

  // Presets
  loadFilterPresets: () => Promise<void>;
  saveFilterPreset: (name: string, icon: FilterPresetIcon) => Promise<void>;
  applyFilterPreset: (presetId: string) => void;
  deleteFilterPreset: (presetId: string) => Promise<void>;
  setPresetAsDefault: (presetId: string, isDefault: boolean) => Promise<void>;
  shareFilterPreset: (presetId: string) => Promise<void>;
  openPresetDialog: () => void;
  closePresetDialog: () => void;

  // Columns
  toggleColumnVisibility: (key: CertColumnKey) => void;
  setColumnOrder: (key: CertColumnKey, order: number) => void;
  setColumnWidth: (key: CertColumnKey, width: number) => void;
  resetColumnConfig: () => void;
  openColumnConfigDialog: () => void;
  closeColumnConfigDialog: () => void;

  // Export
  setExportScope: (scope: 'filtered' | 'all' | 'selected') => void;
  setExportFormat: (format: 'csv' | 'xlsx' | 'pdf' | 'json') => void;
  toggleExportColumn: (key: CertColumnKey) => void;
  setUseCurrentColumnConfig: (value: boolean) => void;

  // Bulk Revoke
  selectAllOnPage: () => void;
  selectAllMatching: () => Promise<void>;
  setRevokeReason: (reason: string) => void;
  setRevokeReasonSubmitted: (submitted: boolean) => void;
  setShowUndoSnackbar: (show: boolean) => void;

  // Search
  addRecentSearch: (query: string) => void;
  clearRecentSearches: () => void;
  setSearching: (searching: boolean) => void;

  // Table Mode
  setTableMode: (mode: 'paginated' | 'virtualized') => void;

  // Grid
  setGridSortField: (field: 'issueDate' | 'recipientName' | 'status') => void;
  setGridDensity: (density: 'comfortable' | 'compact') => void;

  // Real-time
  setWsConnected: (connected: boolean) => void;
  setStaleData: (stale: boolean) => void;
  setNewCertNotification: (notif: { id: string; number: string } | null) => void;
}
```

